  "allow_request_redirects": false,
  "enforce_tls_upstream": true,
  "gateway_may_retry_non_idempotent": false,
  "notes": "Example for the SF International (IECS) sandbox. TENANT-ID-*, CLIENT-ID-* are placeholders: fill in the Gatekeeper tenant ids and the M2M client ids (the sub of the caller's token) when deploying. account-blue and account-green are the ids of the provider_account objects in Gatekeeper and the second part of the handles in the file given to gateway-authz as --sf-openapi-apps (gatekeeper:sfintl-test/account-blue). upstream_hostname and port describe the route's upstream, which is provider-signer, not the carrier; gateway-authz does not read them, nor enforce_tls_upstream (it ignores everything outside the rows' decision fields). enforce_tls_upstream is true because the hop from the gateway to provider-signer is mutual TLS; provider-signer's own hop to the carrier's sandbox is plain HTTP, and this field does not describe it."
